---
/**
 * /contact/ -- a handover.
 *
 * A product is an object and gets a spec sheet; an engagement is a
 * period of time and gets a schedule; a case study is a change of
 * state and gets a ledger. A contact page is a message leaving one
 * desk and landing on another, so all three folds answer a part of
 * that: where it goes, what comes back, and what the call opens with.
 *
 * Two things here are deliberate departures from every other page:
 *
 *   1. No `PageMasthead`. This is the one page whose reader arrives
 *      with intent already formed. Making them scroll past a stand of
 *      facts to reach the field they came to type in is a tax, so the
 *      h1 and the form are the top of the page and the facts sit in
 *      the slip beside it.
 *
 *   2. `cta={false}`. The footer CTA's button is "Book a consultation"
 *      pointing at /contact/, which on /contact/ is a button that
 *      reloads the page. The colophon still renders.
 */
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro';
import ContactForm from '@/components/ui/ContactForm.tsx';

import { organization, orgRef, breadcrumbs, abs } from '@/data/schema';

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'ContactPage',
    '@id': abs('/contact/'),
    url: abs('/contact/'),
    name: 'Contact CloudAlgo',
    mainEntity: orgRef,
    isPartOf: { '@id': abs('/') + '#website' },
    publisher: orgRef,
    inLanguage: 'en',
  },
  organization,
  breadcrumbs([{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Contact' }], abs('/contact/')),
];

---
<Page
  {schema}
  cta={false}
  title="Contact CloudAlgo — Salesforce, MuleSoft and Heroku consulting"
  description="Tell us what your org is doing wrong. One of the two people who would do the work answers in writing within one working day. Half an hour on a call, no deck."
>

  <!-- ── Fold 1: the desk ──────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="desk" aria-labelledby="desk-heading">
    <div class="desk__inner">
      <nav class="desk__crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
          <li><span aria-current="page">Contact</span></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="desk__grid">
        {/* The entrance animation stays on this Astro wrapper. The
            island is inside it, and `anim-fade-up` on a node React
            owns is a hydration race -- see StatsBar.astro. */}
        <div class="desk__col anim-fade-up">
          <h1 id="desk-heading" class="desk__title">Start with the sentence you are <span class="mark mark--draw">tired of saying</span>.</h1>
          <p class="desk__lede">
            &ldquo;We re-key that by hand.&rdquo; &ldquo;The data is a day old.&rdquo; &ldquo;That system
            has no API.&rdquo; Write yours below. It reaches Sandeep and Vikash, the two people who would
            do the work, and one of them answers in writing within one working day.
          </p>

          <ContactForm client:load />
        </div>

        <aside class="slip anim-fade-up" aria-labelledby="slip-heading">
          <h2 id="slip-heading" class="slip__title">Where this lands</h2>

          <dl class="slip__rows">
            <div><dt>Read by</dt><dd>Sandeep Kumar<i>&amp;</i>Vikash Agarwal</dd></div>
            <div><dt>First reply</dt><dd>One working day</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Replies from</dt><dd>sales@cloudalgo.com</dd></div>
            <div><dt>We work in</dt><dd>IST &middot; UTC+5:30</dd></div>
            <div><dt>The call</dt><dd>Half an hour. No deck.</dd></div>
          </dl>

          <div class="slip__direct">
            <a class="slip__line" href="mailto:sales@cloudalgo.com"><span>Write</span>sales@cloudalgo.com</a>
            <a class="slip__line" href="tel:+916377360659"><span>Call</span>+91 6377 360659</a>
            <p class="slip__line slip__line--flat"><span>Find</span>Jaipur, Rajasthan, India</p>
          </div>

          <div class="slip__seal">
            <img src="/salesforce/Salesforce_Partner_Badge_RGB.webp" alt="" width="120" height="84" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <span class="slip__seal-text">Salesforce Consulting Partner<i>since 2019</i></span>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Fold 2: the reply, as an exhibit ──────────────────── -->
  <section class="section-press" aria-labelledby="reply-heading">
    <div class="section-press__head anim-fade-up">
      <h2 id="reply-heading" class="section-title section-title--xs section-title--tighter section-press__title">
        What comes back.
      </h2>
      <span class="section-press__note">A template of the first reply, not a real thread</span>
    </div>

    <div class="reply__spread anim-fade-up">
      <figure class="reply">
        <div class="reply__head">
          <span class="reply__key">From</span><span class="reply__val">Sandeep Kumar or Vikash Agarwal &middot; sales@cloudalgo.com</span>
          <span class="reply__key">Subject</span><span class="reply__val">Re: the sentence you sent us</span>
          <span class="reply__key">Sent</span><span class="reply__val">Within one working day</span>
        </div>

        <ol class="reply__body">
          <li>
            <b>What we think is actually going wrong</b>, in three lines. It is not always the thing you described &mdash; a
            manual step is often a symptom of a permission model nobody has touched since go-live.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Which shape this is</b>: a project with an ending, a retainer, one of our four products, or nothing at all.
            We have talked people out of building things.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>The two or three things we still need to know</b> before anyone could scope it honestly &mdash; usually who
            owns the system on the other side, and whether it will give us an API.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Three times we could talk</b>, half an hour each. If none of them work, say so and we will send three more.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </figure>

      <div class="reply__margin">
        <p class="reply__note"><span>Who writes it</span>One of the two people whose names are on the work. There is no account manager to hand you to.</p>
        <p class="reply__note"><span>What it never contains</span>A proposal you did not ask for, a deck, or a price written before we understand the work.</p>
        <p class="reply__note"><span>If we cannot help</span>We say so in the same reply, and name someone who can. We would rather lose the work than scope something we cannot land.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Fold 3: the questions ─────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section-press" aria-labelledby="asks-heading">
    <div class="section-press__head anim-fade-up">
      <h2 id="asks-heading" class="section-title section-title--xs section-title--tighter section-press__title">
        What we will ask on the call.
      </h2>
      <span class="section-press__note">Five questions &middot; bring the answers and half an hour is enough</span>
    </div>

    <ul class="asks anim-fade-up">
      <li class="asks__row">
        <p class="asks__q">What does the person doing this by hand actually do, step by step?</p>
        <p class="asks__why"><span>Why we ask</span>The step that hurts is rarely the one on the process diagram.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="asks__row">
        <p class="asks__q">How many times a day does it happen, and what does one mistake cost?</p>
        <p class="asks__why"><span>Why we ask</span>This is what decides whether it is worth building at all.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="asks__row">
        <p class="asks__q">What has already been tried, and why did it stop?</p>
        <p class="asks__why"><span>Why we ask</span>What failed last time usually rules out the obvious answer before we start.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="asks__row">
        <p class="asks__q">Who owns the system on the other side, and will they give us an API?</p>
        <p class="asks__why"><span>Why we ask</span>Nothing else moves a delivery date as much as this answer.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="asks__row">
        <p class="asks__q">What has to be true before you would call this finished?</p>
        <p class="asks__why"><span>Why we ask</span>Work with no ending is a retainer, not a project. Better to know now.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    {/* One line on purpose: Astro trims whitespace at a markup boundary,
        so a line break either side of a link welds it to its neighbour. */}
    <p class="asks__foot">If a form is the wrong shape for this, write to <a href="mailto:sales@cloudalgo.com">sales@cloudalgo.com</a> or call <a href="tel:+916377360659">+91 6377 360659</a> &mdash; both reach the same two people. Not ready to talk? <a href="/case-studies/">Read the five case studies</a> instead.</p>
  </section>
</Page>
